# Generated by Cargo
# will have compiled files and executables
debug/
target/
**/target/

# Remove Cargo.lock from gitignore if creating an executable, leave it for libraries
# More information here https://doc.rust-lang.org/cargo/guide/cargo-toml-vs-cargo-lock.html
Cargo.lock
**/Cargo.lock

# These are backup files generated by rustfmt
**/*.rs.bk

# MSVC Windows builds of rustc generate these, which store debugging information
*.pdb
.idea/
.run/
.env
.local/
/Docker/.erlang.cookie
/Doc/.*.drawio.bkp
/**/.DS_Store
src/.DS_Store
/*.profraw
/coverage/*.info
/cobertura.xml
/tarpaulin-report.html
.secrets
# `/scripts/` holds untracked personal helper scripts (e.g. the
# `check-spanish` target's `spanish.py`). The `check_panic_policy.sh`
# enforcement gate (issue #173) and its fixtures ARE tracked — Cargo.toml's
# `include` list has no `scripts/**` glob, so they never ship in the
# published crate either way.
/scripts/*
!/scripts/check_panic_policy.py
!/scripts/panic_policy_fixtures/
!/scripts/panic_policy_fixtures/*.rs
